- Story & Context: Clara, the head projectionist, caught herself staring at the flickering bulb for six hours straight, hallucinating that her own shadow was detached and dancing to the beat of the charango. When asked by an audience member if she was okay, she simply muttered, "I am just the dust in the beam," before launching into a blistering solo that felt like a frantic interrogation of the empty screen.
