Track 3: The Frame-Drop Theory
- Story & Context: Legend says the theater burned down because the bass frequencies became so low they physically vibrated the nitrate film into spontaneous combustion, leaving behind only the charred remains of the band's ledger. Years later, locals claim that if you stand in the ruins, you can still hear the "frequency of the lost reel" ringing in your teeth as a haunting, low-end hum. "Cut the thread and watch the sequence fall away," the choir chants, acknowledging that the music was always destined to destroy the medium that birthed it.
